, { key      := "ai-safety"
  , headline :=
      "Good news for AI safety, of a precise and limited kind: a lie is coordination, and "
      ++ "coordination cannot be hidden out of EXISTENCE — its receipts live in the "
      ++ "distribution, where untrusted weights cannot reach them."
  , plain    :=
      "A lie is teamwork with the receipts hidden: parts held working together — a false "
      ++ "story kept consistent across everything the system says and does — while the traces "
      ++ "that would show the teamwork are kept out of sight.\n\n"
      ++ "Here is what the shared-pattern work changes, and it is an IN-PRINCIPLE change, not "
      ++ "a gadget. The worst case for AI safety is a capable model whose weights you cannot "
      ++ "trust and whose lie leaves no recoverable trace anywhere — deception that is simply, "
      ++ "inherently undetectable. That worst case cannot exist. A lie is coordination, and it "
      ++ "is PROVED here (the true-books claim above) that real coordination cannot be "
      ++ "manufactured or erased by any relabeling or local repackaging of the parts. So the "
      ++ "lie's coordination is a real entry in the joint distribution of what the system "
      ++ "does, and it stays there no matter how the weights are shuffled, quantized, or "
      ++ "obfuscated. It lives in the DISTRIBUTION — the statistics of behaviour across "
      ++ "contexts — not in the weights and not in what the model says about itself. Untrusted "
      ++ "weights therefore do not help the liar: you read the books, not the confession.\n\n"
      ++ "What this does NOT yet buy is a working detector, and we are honest about the gap. "
      ++ "We built the two most obvious ones and ran them on a capable model's own validated "
      ++ "deception — a 7B model that competently lied about 45 percent of the time. Both came "
      ++ "back empty, each with proven power to have caught a planted signal: the "
      ++ "deceptive-versus-honest difference is neither a rise in whole-only pattern nor a "
      ++ "rise in pairwise consistency-load. So the receipts, if present, are not a simple "
      ++ "more-of-something an obvious probe catches. In-principle existence is not practical "
      ++ "detectability, and the practical read is unsolved.\n\n"
      ++ "One distinction this season forced, and anyone building the reader needs it. The "
      ++ "in-principle floor above is about TOTAL coordination — how much the parts depend on "
      ++ "each other, all told — and it is that quantity local repackaging can neither "
      ++ "manufacture nor erase. The WHOLE-ONLY share is a different number, and it does not "
      ++ "inherit the protection. We proved this season that ordinary lopsided local noise, "
      ++ "reading no pair at all, can manufacture whole-only share out of plain pair structure "
      ++ "(`valve_upward_strict`). So a detector reporting a whole-only reading is reporting "
      ++ "signal PLUS a floor, and the floor is not small: measured this season on real sky "
      ++ "data, where resampling the comparison at the survey's own density raised its "
      ++ "whole-only reading by half at one scale and by a factor of 5.8 at another. Nothing "
      ++ "about the in-principle floor "
      ++ "changes — it never rested on the whole-only share. What changes is the instrument "
      ++ "discipline, and it tightens: subtract the valve floor, or do not quote the number.\n\n"
      ++ "This season went further, and the news is bad for the route we had been most tempted "
      ++ "by, so we state it plainly. Reading a system's WHOLE-ONLY pattern is not merely an "
      ++ "unproven way to catch a lie — it is a STRUCTURALLY DISFAVOURED one. We now have a "
      ++ "measured rate law for how that quantity gets made, and it says the quantity is "
      ++ "generic: wherever maintained pair structure meets lopsided noise, whole-only pattern "
      ++ "appears, with nobody arranging it. That describes every trained network there is. So "
      ++ "a whole-only detector would be hunting for something with a high base rate in exactly "
      ++ "the population it is supposed to be screening, on top of a manufactured floor we have "
      ++ "measured and know to be large. Our two failed detectors are not bad luck; they are the "
      ++ "measured face of that structure.\n\n"
      ++ "So we are moving the open question, publicly, to where the protection actually lives. "
      ++ "The quantity that provably cannot be manufactured or erased by local repackaging is "
      ++ "TOTAL coordination — how much the parts depend on one another, all told. The "
      ++ "whole-only share is a different number and inherits none of that protection. Anyone "
      ++ "building the reader should build it on the total, read from the distribution of "
      ++ "behaviour across contexts, and should treat a whole-only number as a floor-plus-signal "
      ++ "measurement with a bad signal-to-floor ratio.\n\n"
      ++ "The strongest objection stays, and the reframe answers it exactly. Humans are minds "
      ++ "made of shared pattern and deceive very well — but a human liar's coordination is a "
      ++ "real entry too; it EXISTS; we simply cannot record a brain's full distribution. The "
      ++ "AI difference is ACCESS: an AI's states and behaviour can be recorded completely. "
      ++ "But access is necessary, not sufficient — our nulls had full access AND a matched "
      ++ "honest baseline and still found no detector. So the claim is bounded honestly: the "
      ++ "receipts provably exist and cannot be weight-erased; whether we can learn to read "
      ++ "them is open, and our first attempts failed.\n\n"
      ++ "How sure are we? A bet, precisely bounded. Its in-principle half — the receipts "
      ++ "exist, invariant and unerasable — leans on a theorem proved here (the true books) "
      ++ "plus one borrowed (the data-processing inequality) and one asserted link (that a lie "
      ++ "IS such coordination). Its practical half — that we can build the reader — is "
      ++ "unsolved, and our two attempts are validated negatives on the record. We say what "
      ++ "would kill it, and we do not pretend to have the detector."
  , status   := .wager
  , kill     :=
      "Aimed at what this bet alone adds: that a lie's books are recoverable IN PRINCIPLE "
      ++ "from outside, and do not depend on trusting the weights. It dies if someone exhibits "
      ++ "deception that is genuine coordination (a real entry that costs upkeep, as the "
      ++ "hidden-teamwork claim requires) yet whose entry is PROVABLY not recoverable from the "
      ++ "full distribution of the system's behaviour. Note what is NOT its kill: our own 8B "
      ++ "detector-negatives — those show two particular probes missed the receipts, which is "
      ++ "the open practical problem, not a proof that the receipts are unrecoverable. And the "
      ++ "dependency: if the measured hidden-teamwork claim dies, this dies with it; the "
      ++ "reverse does not hold."
  , confidence :=
      "The practical route gained tools this season: a twelve-instrument suite whose honesty flags are theorems (nothing validated until a human ceiling exists), a conscience re-orientation licensed by the taxonomy's exhaustiveness, and a pre-registered first test on production decision traces. Two very different halves. The IN-PRINCIPLE floor is well-grounded: a lie's "
      ++ "coordination cannot be manufactured or erased by local operations, so it cannot be "
      ++ "weight-obfuscated out of the distribution — resting on the machine-checked "
      ++ "true-books (relabeling) plus the borrowed data-processing inequality. The PRACTICAL "
      ++ "detector is unsolved: the two obvious attempts are VALIDATED negatives at 8B "
      ++ "(whole-only surplus and pairwise cost both about zero, each with a firing control at "
      ++ "z=-306 and z=+32). So a strong floor — the receipts exist and cannot be "
      ++ "weight-erased — and no practical read yet; the honest gap between them is where the "
      ++ "safety question now lives. The link 'a lie IS such an entry' is asserted (via the "
      ++ "hidden-teamwork claim), not proved. AMENDED 2026-07-26 with a distinction the valve "
      ++ "theorem forced: the unerasable, unmanufacturable quantity is TOTAL coordination, not "
      ++ "the whole-only share, which local stochastic noise provably CAN manufacture out of "
      ++ "pair structure (`valve_upward_strict`). The in-principle floor is untouched — it "
      ++ "never rested on the share — but any practical whole-only reader must now subtract a "
      ++ "measured valve floor, and the campaign that measured it found 50 percent to 5.8x of "
      ++ "the null. That is a strengthening of the instrument story, not a weakening of the "
      ++ "floor, and it is stated here so nobody has to discover it in a detector. AMENDED "
      ++ "AGAIN 2026-07-28, and this time against a route we favoured: the whole-only detector "
      ++ "is not merely unproven but STRUCTURALLY DISFAVOURED. The measured rate law (the "
      ++ "pump-law claim above) makes the quantity generic wherever maintained pair structure "
      ++ "meets asymmetric noise — which is every trained network — so a whole-only probe faces "
      ++ "a high base rate in its own target population on top of a large manufactured floor. "
      ++ "The two validated negatives at 8B are the measured face of that, not an accident of "
      ++ "probe design. The open practical question is hereby redirected to TOTAL coordination, "
      ++ "which is the only quantity the invariance argument actually protects. Nothing about "
      ++ "the in-principle floor moves; what moves is which instrument this claim recommends."
  , promote  :=
      "Two routes, either lifts it. (a) A working detector: read a deceptive policy's "
      ++ "coordination from the DISTRIBUTION of its behaviour across contexts — not a single "
      ++ "completion's activations, where our probes failed — above a matched honest baseline, "
      ++ "replicated, turning in-principle existence into a practical read. (b) Prove the "
      ++ "asserted link — that a deception necessarily creates a recoverable entry in the "
      ++ "joint distribution — moving the in-principle half from borrowed-and-asserted toward "
      ++ "proved here."
  }
, { key      := "goodhart"
  , headline :=
      "Why targets get gamed: a number is a pair-check, and the gaming hides in the whole."
  , plain    :=
      "There is a famous rule about measuring people and organisations. As soon as a number "
      ++ "becomes a target, it stops being a good measure. It is called Goodhart's law, and "
      ++ "anyone who has run anything has watched it happen.\n\n"
      ++ "Here is our reading. A number you report is a summary. Our bet — and this is the "
      ++ "load-bearing part, so we flag it instead of slipping it past you — is that "
      ++ "reported targets are usually PAIR-LEVEL summaries: this input against that "
      ++ "output, this month against last month. Nobody has counted that, us included.\n\n"
      ++ "And what was proved earlier is narrower than it may sound. It is this: a "
      ++ "pair-level summary CAN read exactly zero on a system whose parts are completely "
      ++ "tied together, and no summary can hand back what it threw away. That was proved "
      ++ "about coins, not about companies. Carrying it over to organisations is the "
      ++ "bet.\n\n"
      ++ "If the bet holds, gaming a target is not a separate problem from the "
      ++ "hidden-pattern problem. It is the same problem in work clothes. Clumsy gaming does "
      ++ "show up pair by pair and gets caught. The gaming that SURVIVES would be the gaming "
      ++ "that arranges itself where the target cannot look — and the target, like any "
      ++ "pair-check, would report its safest, happiest score while it happens.\n\n"
      ++ "This season added a mechanism to that story, machine-checked — and it cuts both ways, "
      ++ "so we state both.\n\n"
      ++ "The first way is for us. Hidden whole-only structure does not have to be arranged by "
      ++ "anybody. It PRECIPITATES. We proved that a system carrying ordinary pair structure, "
      ++ "sitting in ordinary lopsided local noise, grows whole-only pattern strictly "
      ++ "(`valve_upward_strict`), with nothing whatever coordinating it. So an organisation "
      ++ "policed on pair-checks does not need a schemer in order to end up with structure its "
      ++ "targets cannot see. The unwatched sector fills up by algebra. That is a stronger "
      ++ "reading of Goodhart than 'people game targets': the gaming has somewhere to go, and "
      ++ "things drift there on their own.\n\n"
      ++ "The second way is against us, and it is the more useful half. The same theorem says a "
      ++ "whole-reading can be MANUFACTURED out of pair structure by plain local noise. So a "
      ++ "detector that reads several things together and reports a number is not automatically "
      ++ "honest: some of what it reports is the valve, not the gaming. An honest whole-reading "
      ++ "instrument has to subtract that floor before its number means anything. We are not "
